<Prose title="Warble and other notch apps" description="What Warble does and doesn't do, and when another Mac notch app is a better fit.">
  <h1>Warble and other notch apps</h1>
  <p>Several Mac apps turn the notch into something useful. Warble does one job: it shows what's playing and lets you control it. This page says what that means, so you can tell whether Warble is the right one for you.</p>

  <h2>Pick Warble if you want</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Music controls and nothing else.</strong> Play, pause, skip, move through a song, change the volume and switch speakers, from a hover or a click.</li>
    <li><strong>An app that stays out of the way.</strong> When nothing's playing, Warble draws nothing and uses no CPU.</li>
    <li><strong>No account, no cloud, no analytics.</strong> It goes online only to check for updates, after it asks, and to find the album cover for a song playing in your browser. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Free, open source software.</strong> The <a href="https://github.com/LorcanChinnock/warble">code is on GitHub</a> under the GPL-3.0 license, with no ads.</li>
    <li><strong>A notch on any Mac.</strong> On a Mac without a notch, or an external display, Warble draws a notch of its own at the top of the screen.</li>
    <li><strong>Any player.</strong> Apple Music, Spotify, podcast apps and video in Safari, Chrome or another browser.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Pick something else if you want</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>More than music.</strong> Warble has no calendar, file shelf, widgets, timers or battery readout. Apps such as <a href="https://github.com/TheBoredTeam/boring.notch">Boring Notch</a>, NotchNook and <a href="https://tryalcove.com">Alcove</a> add some or all of these, and <a href="https://wouter01.github.io/MediaMate">MediaMate</a> focuses on media controls and a replacement for the volume and brightness pop-ups.</li>
    <li><strong>An app that's finished.</strong> Warble is in beta. It works, and it's still being built.</li>
    <li><strong>An app Apple has notarized.</strong> Warble isn't notarized yet, so macOS blocks it the first time you open it, and the <a href="/#install">install steps</a> show how to open it anyway. Notarization is <a href="https://github.com/LorcanChinnock/warble/issues/304">planned</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These other apps change their features and prices, so check each one's own site before you decide.</p>

  <h2>Try it</h2>
  <p>Warble needs macOS 15 or later, on Apple silicon or Intel. Install it with <code>brew install lorcanchinnock/tap/warble</code>, or <a href="/download">download the zip</a>. The <a href="/docs/get-started/">user guide</a> covers the rest.</p>
</Prose>
